# feature-ladder: Hindsight server configuration
# Copy to hindsight.env, fill in the key, then run start-hindsight.sh.
#
# Principle: every LLM call Hindsight makes on its own (fact extraction on
# retain, observation consolidation, knowledge-page / mental-model refresh,
# reflect) runs on the cheapest model that does that job correctly.
# Extraction and consolidation are summarisation jobs -> Haiku.
# Reflect is a multi-step reasoning loop that domain experts rely on -> Sonnet
# (drop it to Haiku too if you find the answers good enough for your repos).
#
# Per-operation overrides follow Hindsight's pattern:
#   HINDSIGHT_API_<OP>_LLM_PROVIDER / _MODEL / _API_KEY
#   where <OP> is RETAIN, REFLECT, CONSOLIDATION or MENTAL_MODEL_REFRESH.
#   Mental-model (knowledge page) refresh inherits the REFLECT chain unless set.

# --- Global default (used by any operation without an override) -------------
HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5
HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_API_KEY=sk-ant-REPLACE_ME

# --- Retain: fact extraction (highest volume, pure summarisation) -------------
HINDSIGHT_API_RETAIN_LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
HINDSIGHT_API_RETAIN_LLM_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5
# Haiku supports long outputs, so the default 65k retain completion budget is fine.
# If you ever switch retain to a model capped at <=32k output tokens, lower this
# and keep it above HINDSIGHT_API_RETAIN_CHUNK_SIZE (default 3000):
# HINDSIGHT_API_RETAIN_MAX_COMPLETION_TOKENS=16000

# --- Consolidation: merging facts into observations (summarisation) -----------
HINDSIGHT_API_CONSOLIDATION_LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
HINDSIGHT_API_CONSOLIDATION_LLM_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5

# --- Mental model / knowledge page refresh (summarisation, delta mode) --------
HINDSIGHT_API_MENTAL_MODEL_REFRESH_LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
HINDSIGHT_API_MENTAL_MODEL_REFRESH_LLM_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5

# --- Reflect: agentic reasoning over memory (used by domain experts) ----------
HINDSIGHT_API_REFLECT_LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
HINDSIGHT_API_REFLECT_LLM_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
# Cheapest alternative if Sonnet quality is not needed:
# HINDSIGHT_API_REFLECT_LLM_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5

# --- Subscription instead of API key (LOCAL, PERSONAL USE ONLY) ---------------
# Hindsight's docs say the claude-code provider is for local personal dev only
# (not Docker/servers/shared hosts) and counts against Pro/Max limits. If you
# run Hindsight bare-metal (pip) on your own workstation you may use:
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_PROVIDER=claude-code
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5
# (run `claude setup-token` and put the sk-ant-oat01- token in HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_API_KEY)

# --- Ports / storage ----------------------------------------------------------
HINDSIGHT_API_PORT=8888

# --- Optional: protect the MCP endpoint ---------------------------------------
# HINDSIGHT_API_TENANT_EXTENSION=hindsight_api.extensions.builtin.tenant:ApiKeyTenantExtension
# HINDSIGHT_API_TENANT_API_KEY=choose-a-secret
# (then export HINDSIGHT_API_KEY=choose-a-secret in the shell that runs Claude Code)

# --- Optional: tell agents which tags to use, via tool descriptions -----------
HINDSIGHT_API_MCP_INSTRUCTIONS=Tag every memory with project:<name> and feature:<slug>; one fact per retain.
